# Project rules (always apply)

Follow project invariants on every change. Full text: @docs/rules.md

1. Keep `make check` green.
2. Do not run cloud-cost commands (deploys, BQ queries, pipeline runs) — human-only.
3. No secrets or JSON service-account keys in commits.
4. YAGNI / reuse / fewest files; fix root cause once (global ponytail User Rule).
5. Consult @docs/memory.md before reversing decisions; append notable new ones.
6. Every change reaches `main` by pull request. `main` is branch-protected and a merge deploys.
7. Stacked PRs — one concern per PR; base on the dependency branch; retarget to `main` after the base merges.
8. Prefer `feat|fix|test|ci|chore|docs(scope): …` commits.
